; the middle arguments of a binder -- the range of `sum i (a, b) T`, the point of `lim v a T` --
; are outside the scope of its variable, as in mathematics: in `sum x (0, n) (sum x (0, x) x)`,
; the inner range `(0, x)` is the outer `x` (decided 2026-10-05; before, every argument of a
; binder was inside its scope, and the kernel was inconsistent about it)
load analysis
const n, f
arity f 1

; "sum-last" substitutes the outer x also into the range of the inner sum
(sum x (0, n + 1) (sum x (0, x) x)) = (sum x (0, n + 1) x) + (sum x (0, n) (sum x (0, x) x))

; instantiating a ∀ with the name of the binder: no capture, the range is outside
use ∀ y ((sum x (0, y) x) = f y)
(sum x (0, n) x) = f n
(sum x (0, x) x) = f x

; the outer w is the range of the sum, the inner w its variable: instantiating the outer one
; replaces the range only
use ∀ w ((sum w (0, w) w) = 5)
(sum w (0, 3) w) = 5
(sum v (0, 3) v) = 5
